<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhou Fohai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1897–1948</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhou Fohai (1897–1948) was a Chinese politician who attended the founding congress of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a> in 1921 before joining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a>. In 1940 he followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-jingwei">Wang Jingwei</a> into the Japanese-backed Reorganised National Government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>, where he controlled its finances. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s surrender he was convicted of treason; his death sentence was commuted to life imprisonment, and he died in prison in 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhou-fohai.jpg" alt="Zhou Fohai" width="320" height="362" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown; scanned by 天竺鼠 (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zhou_Fohai.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
